DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((e^(x)))^(1/3)");
$fun_1 = Formula("((x/1))^2");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(-infinity, 12] U {-8, -7, 2, 4, 6, 7}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("((-infinity, 12]) U (6, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[1, 6] U {-3, -2} U [1, 11] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 11])");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-3, -2} U [1, 11]");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-3, -2} - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 6])) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (((([1, 11]) U {-3, -2} - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 11])) U {-3, -2}))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 11])");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`16+15-18-5/16`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(12.6875),width=>7}
---

[`12+19-17`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(14.),width=>3}
---

What is the value of [`5+6-7-18`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(-14.),width=>9}
---

What is the value of [`18+6-5+19*18`]? [_____]{Formula('361')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-3, -2\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 6\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 11\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A \cup C \cap C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(A \cap B) \cap ((((C) \cup A \cap C) \cup A)) \cap C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, -7, 2, 4, 6, 7\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 5\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \leq 12\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`(C) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 9, -7, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 0, -4, 1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -7, 3>") . Compute("<0, -4, 1>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<0, -4, 1>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, -4, 1>") x Compute("<9, -7, 3>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -7, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, -8, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, 6, -10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, -8, -9>") x Compute("<-3, 6, -10>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-3, 6, -10>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 6, -10>") x Compute("<-8, -8, -9>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-8, -8, -9>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
